When $\frac{13-\sqrt{131}}{4}$ is substituted for $x$ in the quadratic equation $2x^2-13x+k=0$, we get:

\begin{align*}
2\left(\frac{13-\sqrt{131}}{4}\right)^2 - 13\left(\frac{13-\sqrt{131}}{4}\right) + k &= 0\\
2\left(\frac{(13-\sqrt{131})^2}{16}\right) - \frac{13(13-\sqrt{131})}{4} + k &= 0\\
\end{align*}

This is the equation formed when $\frac{13-\sqrt{131}}{4}$ is substituted for $x$ in the quadratic equation.
